{"authored" [{"question" "q-321299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/assets/6fe3721ff3ab63e75be934c79b03d4ca601513c2e08b987a0bafd94c74856e90.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=a+\\lambda b$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/assets/9c8d67718152bc1bc9569213369580b6fc6f5bc1fe0c63b637f14c9f659dfe27.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=\\frac{2}{3}|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=\\frac{2}{3}b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{2}{3}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+\\frac{2}{3}b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\lambda =\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4e80d7502e27fd33982c3fb6f834c31333acc979c09703bef348ea980101a64" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-321299" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/assets/1d424b5db0534a8d9abc9b0aa84dcb2e6860a7ed51de7390fc4f7e91c1c33f2b.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+4b,$ find $\\lambda .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+4b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $4b.$ So, we first draw the vector $4b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/assets/d8fdfb800bd9bbb179d51115b86823d99029732fee9810281b9c587a32376993.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $4b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=4|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-4a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =4b-4a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+4b=-4a+4b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-4\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4e80d7502e27fd33982c3fb6f834c31333acc979c09703bef348ea980101a64" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-367052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "va