\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-2b-\\frac{1}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-2b=-\\frac{1}{2}a-2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120257" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4e80d7502e27fd33982c3fb6f834c31333acc979c09703bef348ea980101a64" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120257" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db377