ture above. If $i=\\lambda j+\\mu k$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/assets/cb8209592ec6d5be435622999c1b3eb86e1756cbe9852be0efdbbf41d41777ff.png)\n\nIn $△OJL$ shown above, we have  \n\n- $OJ=2|j|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}$ and $j$ have the opposite direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=-2j.$  \n\nSimilarly:  \n\n- $JL=|k|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{JL}$ and $k$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{JL}=k.$  \n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\ni=\\overset{\\to }{OJ}+\\overset{\\to }{JL}=-2j+k.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $i=\\lambda j+\\mu k=-2j+k.$  \n\nSince $j∦k,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way.  Equating the coefficients, we get \n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2,\\,\\mu =1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4e80d7502e27fd33982c3fb6f834c31333acc979c09703bef348ea980101a64" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19370" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/assets/601e049067de307ef2321ae9b516d1c7306d837ca0758c080074446a8c54389d.png)\n\nIn $△OAC$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OA=2|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OA}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=2a.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $AC=2|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=2b.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =2a+2b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+\\mu b=2a+2b.$ \n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19370" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4e80d7502e27fd33982c3fb6f834c31333acc979c09703bef348ea980101a64" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19370" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/assets/36742531a5f9f5d77c5f7e90980120479f4142cecaf6e84937d76d938688409d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=d,$ $\\overset{\\to }{ON}=e,$ and $T$ divides $\\overset{―}{MN}$ in the ratio $MT:TN=8:3.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OT}$ via the vectors $d$ and $e.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OT}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$d+$\n{{field-2}}\n$e$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=d,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{MT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OMN,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{MN} & =\\overset{\\to }{MO}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-d+e \\\\  & =e-d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $MT:TN=8:3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{MT}=\\frac{8}{11}\\overset{\\to }{MN}=\\frac{8}{11}(e-d).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT} \\\\  & =d+\\frac{8}{11}(e-d) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{11}d+\\frac{8}{11}e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4e80d7502e27fd33982c3fb6f834c31333acc979c09703bef348ea980101a64" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/assets/040127594f639248736d4492f1853bcb1e6ef18c37db9242ebe466045713628a.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OV}=v$ and $W$ divides $\\overset{―}{UV}$ in the ratio $UW:WV=2:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OW}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{UW}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OUV,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\\overset{\\to }{UO}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-u+v \\\\  & =v-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $UW:WV=2:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{UW}=\\frac{2}{9}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=\\frac{2}{9}(v-u).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OW} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =u+\\frac{2}{9}(v-u) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}u+\\frac{2}{9}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e4e80d7502e27fd33982c3fb6f834c31333acc979c09703bef348ea980101a64" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=-\\frac{1}{3}v+\\frac{2}{3}u"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc54df5c87f5dd569379a85e19d17b5db3774493db711a68a1e15485b9829a3b" "basis" 348 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13931259/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\fra