demy/question-capture/13981901/state.json" "file_sha256" "9753d6604ac55790e729dbaf40ab636d10bc4542adbf92a8cbe46357a16a25b0" "basis" 900 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-325983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/assets/646b8f1322f815e786f82eb8cfb3fa9e84a3c8d588c94910b0b702b607bfb2d8.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{3}{2}|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-\\frac{3}{2}a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-2b-\\frac{3}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-2b=-\\frac{3}{2}a-2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/state.json" "file_sha256" "9753d6604ac55790e729dbaf40ab636d10bc4542adbf92a8cbe46357a16a25b0" "basis" 900 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-325983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b4476aeb61c12d8e89fd68a7bbc8e33f29f7cb8ca4f1cc18fc60380fae96ce2b" "basis" 900 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-325983" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/state.json" "file_sha256" "9753d6604ac55790e729dbaf40ab636d10bc4542adbf92a8cbe46357a16a25b0" "basis" 900 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-325983" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/state.json" "file_sha256" "9753d6604ac55790e729dbaf40ab636d10bc4542adbf92a8cbe46357a16a25b0" "basis" 900 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981901/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-19338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/816c4ecbfe49321bc6b2bc0d72eb61d6ddd1aeae7e76a275df0975439dde5865.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=a+\\lambda b,$ find $\\lambda .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/6782f2fa59056afd9022edbaf69c44a991bf12a7ac6a190bea3cc08fc7a4996c.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=2.5|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.5b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+2.5b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+2.5b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2.5\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad534175e77d374dcb4f648bb962cc45896f56ca9dcb4ac16dd34918e0fa4f70"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2.5"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-19338" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:an