 $j$ have the opposite direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=-2j.$  \n\nSimilarly:  \n\n- $JL=|k|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{JL}$ and $k$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{JL}=k.$  \n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\ni=\\overset{\\to }{OJ}+\\overset{\\to }{JL}=-2j+k.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $i=\\lambda j+\\mu k=-2j+k.$  \n\nSince $j∦k,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way.  Equating the coefficients, we get \n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2,\\,\\mu =1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad534175e77d374dcb4f648bb962cc45896f56ca9dcb4ac16dd34918e0fa4f70"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-327075" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/36742531a5f9f5d77c5f7e90980120479f4142cecaf6e84937d76d938688409d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=d,$ $\\overset{\\to }{ON}=e,$ and $T$ divides $\\overset{―}{MN}$ in the ratio $MT:TN=8:3.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OT}$ via the vectors $d$ and $e.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OT}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$d+$\n{{field-2}}\n$e$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OT}=\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=d,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{MT}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OMN,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{MN} & =\\overset{\\to }{MO}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-d+e \\\\  & =e-d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $MT:TN=8:3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{MT}=\\frac{8}{11}\\overset{\\to }{MN}=\\frac{8}{11}(e-d).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OT} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MT} \\\\  & =d+\\frac{8}{11}(e-d) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{11}d+\\frac{8}{11}e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad534175e77d374dcb4f648bb962cc45896f56ca9dcb4ac16dd34918e0fa4f70"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322576" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/7e92a09f8448f4d320f86656bc0774e6167b96156041c32eb7a64ba5e8820128.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OD}=d,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OE}=e,$ and $F$ divides $\\overset{―}{DE}$ in the ratio $DF:FE=3:4.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OF}$ via the vectors $d$ and $e.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OF}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$d+$\n{{field-2}}\n$e$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OF}=\\overset{\\to }{OD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OD}=d,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{DF}.$\n\nFirst, from $△ODE,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =\\overset{\\to }{DO}+\\overset{\\to }{OE} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OD}+\\overset{\\to }{OE} \\\\  & =-d+e \\\\  & =e-d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $DF:FE=3:4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{DF}=\\frac{3}{7}\\overset{\\to }{DE}=\\frac{3}{7}(e-d).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OF} & =\\overset{\\to }{OD}+\\overset{\\to }{DF} \\\\  & =d+\\frac{3}{7}(e-d) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}d+\\frac{3}{7}e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322568" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad534175e77d374dcb4f648bb962cc45896f56ca9