rence/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OY}=\\overset{\\to }{OK}+\\overset{\\to }{KY}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OK}=k,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{KY}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OKZ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{KZ} & =\\overset{\\to }{KO}+\\overset{\\to }{OZ} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OK}+\\overset{\\to }{OZ} \\\\  & =-k+z \\\\  & =z-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $KY:YZ=10:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{KY}=\\frac{10}{17}\\overset{\\to }{KZ}=\\frac{10}{17}(z-k).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OY} & =\\overset{\\to }{OK}+\\overset{\\to }{KY} \\\\  & =k+\\frac{10}{17}(z-k) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{17}k+\\frac{10}{17}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad534175e77d374dcb4f648bb962cc45896f56ca9dcb4ac16dd34918e0fa4f70"} {"question" "q-322582" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322582" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{17}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322582" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-322582" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10}{17}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-120304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/6560a7f05ae95638cbfe902dfa022b2d8de6b07c6e1e6f85051ccf87b92ec338.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=i$ and $J$ divides $\\overset{―}{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=5:3.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-120304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OHI,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HI} & =\\overset{\\to }{HO}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-h+i \\\\  & =i-h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $HJ:JI=5:3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{HJ}=\\frac{5}{8}\\overset{\\to }{HI}=\\frac{5}{8}(i-h).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ} \\\\  & =h+\\frac{5}{8}(i-h) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}h+\\frac{5}{8}i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-120304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ad534175e77d374dcb4f648bb962cc45896f56ca9dcb4ac16dd34918e0fa4f70"} {"question" "q-120304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-120304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{1}{2}h+\\frac{1}{2}i"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{1}{8}h+\\frac{3}{4}i"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{4}h+\\frac{1}{4}i"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{8}h+\\frac{5}{8}i"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{5}{8}h+\\frac{3}{8}i"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-120304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{8}h+\\frac{5}{8}i"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-42669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/assets/040127594f639248736d4492f1853bcb1e6ef18c37db9242ebe466045713628a.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OV}=v$ and $W$ divides $\\overset{―}{UV}$ in the ratio $UW:WV=2:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OW}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-42669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=u,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{UW}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OUV,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\\overset{\\to }{UO}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{OV} \\\\  & =-u+v \\\\  & =v-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $UW:WV=2:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{UW}=\\frac{2}{9}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=\\frac{2}{9}(v-u).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OW} & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =u+\\frac{2}{9}(v-u) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{9}u+\\frac{2}{9}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041137/state.json" "file_sha256" "7d2559e12ac5cac60589db9a1a4fec1d29173ce0f4bcc47f3d156606a84e60b4"} {"question" "q-42669" "fi